8 This feature on AlgoTest allows you to execute your entry orders via Market or Limit Order.
9 It is a type of order that allows the order to be executed at the best available price in the market at that time. Market orders lead to high slippage as compared to limit orders. In this feature, no order is sent to your broker in advance. The system fires a market order as soon as your entry condition is met.
10 You can select market order by selecting from the drop-down on Entry Order Type as shown in the image below.
11 The order will not be placed on the broker's end. It will be on the AlgoTest end. As soon as the entry condition is met, Algo will send the order to the broker to execute it.
12 A limit order is a type of order that allows the order to be executed within a specified limit price only. They can help you to reduce slippage. In this feature, a Limit/SL-L order, with the defined trigger & limit price, will be sent to your broker and shall be placed in the order book of your broker either in advance or at the time of the conditi
13 You can select Limit Order from the drop-down on Entry Order Type as shown in the image below.
14 A SL-L order needs to define its trigger and the limit price. Trigger price is the price at which your buy or sell order becomes active for execution. Once the price of the option hits the trigger price set by you, a limit order, with the price set by you, becomes active for execution on the exchange servers. You can enter the Trigger/Limit buffer 
15 Let us understand this with a simple example
16 Nifty ATM Price at 09:20 is 100
17 Entry on Momentum Up = 10 Points
18 In this case, a SL-L order will be placed in your broker's order book as follows: Trigger price = 110 - 2 = ₹ 108 & Limit Price = 110 + 3 = Rs 113. This means that as soon as the LTP breaches trigger a price of Rs 108 a Limit order of Rs 113 becomes active for execution on the exchange servers.
19 Entry Limit/SL-L orders (How they work)​
20 Positions can be entered using Limit/SL-L orders. The order settings will be as follows:
21 Time-Based Entry: A Limit order based on the LTP along with the limit buffer is sent at the time of entry. The Limit Buffer is added in case of a Buy order while the Limit Buffer is subtracted in case of a Sell order.
22 Simple Momentum: Based on your condition a Limit or a SL-L order is sent in advance to your broker
23 Simple Momentum up (instrument) + BUY = SL-L order is placed in advance based on the Trigger and Limit buffer
24 Simple Momentum down (instrument) + SELL = SL-L order is placed in advance based on Trigger and Limit buffer
25 Simple Momentum up (instrument) + SELL = Limit order is placed in advance without any buffer
26 Simple Momentum Down (instrument) + BUY = Limit order is placed in advance without any buffer
27 infoAll Simple Momentum strategies based on underlying points are entered via Limit order with a limit buffer as soon as the entry condition is met.
28 Re-Entry on Tgt/SL: All Re-entry orders are either placed in advance or a Limit order is sent at the time of the condition being met.
29 Re-Cost: Limit/SL-L order sent in advance to your broker.
30 Re-ASAP: A limit order with a limit buffer is sent as soon as the previous leg exits.
31 Re-Momentum on Instrument: Limit/SL-L order sent in advance to your broker based on the set momentum as soon as the previous leg exits.
32 infoStrategies that are based on the underlying are entered via a Limit order as soon as the Re-entry condition is met.
33 Range Breakout: All Range Breakout strategies that are based on the instrument have a Limit/SL-L order sent to your broker as soon as the range time ends. For strategies that are based on the underlying a Limit order is sent as soon as the break condition is met.
34 Make sure that your limit and trigger buffer does not lead to a NEGATIVE limit or Trigger price. In such a case the limit order will be rejected and we will enter the position via Market order.
35 You can enter 0 to 20 seconds to convert to the market after time. This timer is used for converting to the market order when your Limit order skips or your Limit order is partially filled. It operates as follows:
36 Price at 09:20 is 100, Momentum Up = 10 Points
37 Trigger buffer = 0 pts, Trigger Price = Rs 110
